KG42.register("rules-f6f8ed9907fa76bedc075efa",{"id":"03-bilateral_p2p::v141-c-R001","paper":"03-bilateral_p2p","record":{"rule_id":"v141-c-R001","mechanism_id":"v141-a-M01","name":"Demand submission","process_stage":"bidding","market_meaning":"Buyers request discrete-quantity energy trades from potential sellers by making progressively higher price offers during the price-adjustment process. Scope: Buyer offers in the bilateral contract-network price-adjustment process, in both forward and real-time markets.","independence_rationale":"Relations governed by the approved function bidding.demand under the fixed relation-ownership template. Conditional branches retain their explicit scope in local constraints.","V":["bidding.demand"],"E":[],"omega":{"market_type":"DEM","network_level":null,"jurisdiction":null,"pricing_scope":null,"time_scale":null,"participant_types":[],"trading_stage":"bidding","context_text":"Buyer offers in the bilateral contract-network price-adjustment process, in both forward and real-time markets.","unknown_fields":["network_level","jurisdiction","pricing_scope","time_scale","participant_types"],"evidence_ids":["v141-b-g01-e09","v141-b-g02-E19"]},"x":[],"theta":[],"phi":[{"constraint_id":"v141-c-R001-C001","kind":"procedural","role":"core","statement":"Buyers request discrete-quantity energy trades from potential sellers by making progressively higher price offers during the price-adjustment process. Scope: Buyer offers in the bilateral contract-network price-adjustment process, in both forward and real-time markets.","expression":null,"formalization_origin":"not_formalized","template_id":null,"members":["bidding.demand"],"variable_refs":[],"parameter_refs":[],"evidence_ids":["v141-b-g01-e09","v141-b-g02-E19"]}],"pi":[{"evidence_id":"v141-b-g01-e09","location":{"location_id":"src-4a31f0141b-p03-c1r4__v141-a-M01-participation","page":3,"printed_page":null,"section":"II. Contract Networks for Energy Trading","anchor_text":"This paper proposes forward and real-time P2P energy markets, each consisting of energy contracts tr","equation_id":null,"figure_id":null,"table_id":null,"image_ref":"pages/page-03.png","occurrence_role":"definition"},"source_text":"This paper proposes forward and real-time P2P energy markets, each consisting of energy contracts traded between autonomous agents. Three types of agents are considered: 1) 'prosumers', which have a combination of inflexible loads, flexible loads and/or local renewable sources, 2) 'suppliers', which act as intermediaries and 3) 'generators' with traditional fuel-based sources. In the literature, agents fulfilling the suppliers' intermediary role are sometimes referred to as aggregators (e.g., [29]). The potential trading relationships between the agents are described by a contract network. Each energy contract specifies the price of a discrete quantity of energy offered by one agent to another. Physical and informational restrictions on which agents can trade with one another are reflected by the topology of the contract network."},{"evidence_id":"v141-b-g02-E19","location":{"location_id":"src-4a31f0141b-p06-c2r1__v141-a-M01-pricing","page":6,"printed_page":"2031","section":"IV. Price-Adjustment Process","anchor_text":"ENERGY TRADING 2031 al- The process is scalable, since, at each iteration, only the lowest price rem","equation_id":null,"figure_id":null,"table_id":null,"image_ref":"pages/page-06.png","occurrence_role":"unknown"},"source_text":"The process is scalable, since, at each iteration, only the lowest price remaining upstream contract and highest price remaining downstream need to be considered, and the number of available contracts is reduced. ... The price-adjustment process is completed for the forward and real-time markets, so that in each market, the agents agree on a network of contracts which none of them wish to mutually deviate from. The price-adjustment process is constructed with buyers making progressively higher offers for trades to potential sellers, and sellers choosing to accept or reject the offers they receive."}],"field_notes":{"empty_E_reason":"C explicitly supplied only source-backed unary facts for this function; other graph gaps remain reviewable.","empty_x_reason":"No source-supported design-selection or operational variable is declared for this rule. The nearest quantitative object, the buyer price of a trade p^b_omega, is introduced in the price-adjustment setup and price-update evidence (v141-b-g02-E15 and v141-b-g02-E17), whose candidate nodes include pricing.local and coordination.price_signal, not the frozen single node bidding.demand. Declaring it here would require a graph revision or cross-rule fact movement.","empty_theta_reason":"No fixed parameter for demand submission is defined in the supplied evidence for this rule. The price-adjustment increment Delta-p is defined in v141-b-g02-E15 under the price-adjustment process and belongs to pricing/coordination ownership; treating it as a theta of bidding.demand would require adding nodes or edges that are not present in the frozen graph."},"evidence_basis":"explicit","implementation_status":"unimplemented","status":"needs_review","lead_ids":["v141-a-M01-bidding","v141-a-M01-coordination","v141-a-M01-matching","v141-a-M01-participation","v141-a-M01-pricing"],"extras":{"decision_anchor":"bidding.demand","graph_fact_supports":[[{"evidence_id":"v141-b-g02-E19","quote":"The price-adjustment process is completed for the forward and real-time markets, so that in each market, the agents agree on a network of contracts which none of them wish to mutually deviate from. The price-adjustment process is constructed with buyers making progressively higher offers for trades to potential sellers, and sellers choosing to accept or reject the offers they receive."},{"evidence_id":"v141-b-g01-e09","quote":"Each energy contract specifies the price of a discrete quantity of energy offered by one agent to another."}]],"C2_formalization":{"graph_sha256":"906b16066301e2e2089cb7c72ae4cec39e02d0ff2820547720f5bd8ae2f82682","applicability":"non_mathematical","reason":"The frozen rule is a buyer-side process requirement for the bilateral contract-network price-adjustment mechanism. The supplied evidence states that buyers make progressively higher offers for trades to potential sellers and that each contract specifies the price of a discrete quantity of energy, but it does not supply an equation defining a demand-submission function under the single node bidding.demand. The related quantitative price-update equation and state objects are assigned in the graph inventory to pricing/coordination rules and nodes, not to this rule's frozen V/E. Formalizing them here would move facts across rules and exceed the frozen graph. Therefore x and theta remain empty, and the existing core constraint remains not_formalized. This is a rule-scope finding, not a claim that the source lacks mathematical content. The B evidence used here remains unreviewed in this experiment.","bindings":[{"object_id":"v141-c-R001-C001","node_ids":["bidding.demand"],"edge_ids":[],"rationale":"The existing C.1 core procedural constraint describes the buyer-side demand-submission behavior owned by the only frozen node, bidding.demand. No edge exists in the frozen graph for this rule; the rule was assembled as a unary relation. The buyer price-adjustment relations in the source belong to other graph rules/nodes."}],"revision_requests":["If the quantitative offer-price dynamics are to be formalized under R001, C.1 must add pricing.local and/or coordination.price_signal nodes and the associated buyer/seller price state objects and edges, because the price-adjustment update evidence (v141-b-g02-E15 through v141-b-g02-E18) is presently owned by other rules, not by the single bidding.demand node in this frozen graph.","If R001 is intended to cover the buyer-side selection equations from the price-adjustment iteration, C.1 must expose Y_mi, Z_mi, Y*_mi = C^B_mi(Y_mi | Z_mi), buyer price p^b_omega, and the price-adjustment increment Delta-p as typed objects owned by this rule, or add explicit edges/ownership so they can be referenced without cross-rule reuse.","The B evidence for this rule is unreviewed in this experiment; no independent source audit or C2 review has been performed, so this patch does not assert verified source correctness or a verified mathematical expression."]}},"quarantined_references":[]}});
